What is a Proxy?

In general, a proxy means someone or something that acts on behalf of another.

Think of it as a middleman.

Instead of talking directly to someone, you talk to the proxy, and the proxy communicates for you.

Real-Life Example

Imagine you want to meet your school principal.

You don't usually go directly to the principal.

Instead:

You
   │
   ▼
Receptionist (Proxy)
   │
   ▼
Principal

The receptionist acts as a proxy.

=====


In AI

A User Proxy is an AI component that acts on behalf of the user.

Instead of the user directly interacting with every agent, the User Proxy receives the user's request and coordinates with other agents.

Example

You ask:

"Find the best hotel in Chennai."

Without a proxy:

User
   │
   ▼
Travel Agent

With a User Proxy:

User
   │
   ▼
User Proxy
   │
   ▼
Travel Agent
   │
   ▼
Hotel Recommendation

The User Proxy receives your request and passes it to the appropriate agent.

========

What is RetrieveUserProxy?

In Microsoft AutoGen, RetrieveUserProxyAgent is a special type of User Proxy.

It doesn't just forward your message—it can also retrieve information from documents or a knowledge base before asking the LLM to respond.

This is commonly used in RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) systems.

=======

Example with RAG

Suppose you have a PDF:

Restaurant_Menu.pdf

User asks:

"How much is the Chicken Biryani?"

The workflow is:

User
   │
   ▼
RetrieveUserProxy
   │
   ├── Searches the PDF
   │
   ▼
Assistant Agent
   │
   ▼
Answer:
Chicken Biryani costs ₹250.

The RetrieveUserProxy first finds the relevant information, then the assistant uses it to answer.

=======


Why is it called "Retrieve"?

Because it retrieves information from sources such as:

📄 PDF files
📊 CSV files
📝 Text documents
🗄️ Vector databases (FAISS, ChromaDB, Pinecone, etc.)
🌐 Other knowledge sources

before asking the LLM to generate a response.

=======


Two Agents + RetrieveUserProxy

Suppose you have two agents:

Agent 1

Assistant Agent

Answers questions
Plans tasks
Writes code

↓

Agent 2

RetrieveUserProxy

Searches documents
Finds relevant information
Sends that information to the Assistant Agent

The workflow becomes:

User
   │
   ▼
RetrieveUserProxy
(Searches documents)
   │
   ▼
Assistant Agent
(Uses retrieved information)
   │
   ▼
Final Answer

